# The working tree is edited on Windows but executed inside a Linux dev
# container that bind-mounts it directly. With core.autocrlf=true and no rules
# here, git rewrites checked-out text files to CRLF, and a CRLF shell script
# fails in the container with "$'\r': command not found" -- likewise psql -f on
# a .sql file and mongosh on a .js file.
#
# Normalise to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched by end-of-line conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
